{
  "dom_id": "step-e9704",
  "name": "Example: Calculating the Speed of an Object",
  "problem": "At full speed, a fully grown cheetah can cover a distance of $998$ feet in $10$ seconds. What is the speed of the cheetah when running at full speed?",
  "worked_solution": "Speed is a special unit rate applied to moving objects. It is defined as *the distance traveled per unit of time*:\n\n$$\n\\text{speed} = \\dfrac{\\text{distance}}{\\text{time}}\n$$\n\nTo find the speed in feet per second, we divide the number of feet, $998,$ by the number of seconds, $10.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{998}{10} & =99.8.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the speed of the cheetah is $99.8$ feet per second.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "result": null,
